= Why every infinity and finite support maps correctly

== The same monic quintic chart
For a simple branch a, let L=F'(a),H(z)=z⁶F(a+1/z),w=L/(x-a),
V=yw³/L and G(w)=L⁴H(w/L). G is a smooth monic quintic, with constant
L⁴. The inverse is x=a+L/w,y=VL/w³. The unique quintic infinity W is
the old branch point; the old infinities map to B±=(w0,V=±L²).
Thus div(w)=B+ + B- -2W and Q-=-Q+ in Picard. The chart is over
F101⁶; plain coefficient Frobenius is not asserted to fix its class images.
[pcc:unverified]

For u=x²+b x+c,A=u(a), the support is
U=w²+L(2a+b)w/A+L²/A. For u=x+u0 it is U=w+L/(a+u0).
The ordinate is the remainder of v1w²+v(a)w³/L moduloU. These identities
hold in the finite support algebra,including repeated jets. Every actual
denominator and transformed curve equation is checked;no class is dropped.
[pcc:unverified]

An input means Dfin+(n-1)infinity+ +(1-m-n)infinity-. Its transformed
finite ordinary class is Fclass=[Dfin'-mW]. The principal-divisor relation
gives the exact total Fclass+(2n+m-2)Q+. No torsion-free point-group or
division-by2 assumption is used. The global isomorphism/Picard proof is
FULL_CLASS_REPLAY_PROOF.md/PCCb71a87. Existing kernel-only40a568 stays
immutable and keeps its earlier scope. [pcc:unverified]

